# Configure Application in AKS

## 🎯 Objective:
Deploy a containerized application to **Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS)** and expose it using different Kubernetes service types — focusing on **LoadBalancer** for public access.

## 🛠️ Steps to Configure and Expose Application in AKS

### 1. Get AKS Cluster Credentials
Make sure you are logged into Azure CLI:
```bash
az login
az aks get-credentials --resource-group <your-resource-group> --name <your-aks-cluster-name>

### 2. Create Deployment YAML for Your App

apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: sample-app
spec:
  replicas: 2
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: sample
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: sample
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: sample-container
        image: nginx
        ports:
        - containerPort: 80

### 3. Expose the Deployment via LoadBalancer

apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: sample-service
spec:
  type: LoadBalancer
  selector:
    app: sample
  ports:
  - port: 80
    targetPort: 80

### 4. Check the Service and Get External IP

kubectl get svc


